A||||18||Ray Heath||Aftermarket headers
Z||000000||Ray Heath||06-24-99||08:16 PM||||Has anyone installed any of the aftermarket headers on their 2.8. I am in the middle of the 3.4 upgrade to replace the 2.8 and need a recommendation on headers.
Z||000001||Racer 1||06-25-99||01:57 PM||||Hooker Headers might make one for the 2.8.I have Hooker super competion headers on my 2.5.Call Summit Racing and ask if they can get you the headers 4 you car!
Z||000002||mwbackus||06-25-99||04:01 PM||||If hooker actually does make cheap headers for the fiero V6, I know of about 100 people that will be wetting their pants because they spent over $500 for their set.  Seriously though, fiero V6 headers are a special animal due the cramped area they have to exist in, and the angle they need to use for the over trans. crossover.  Here are the companies that offer Fiero V6 headers that I know of:<p>The Fiero Store  <br>http://www.fierostore.com<br>These are not considered to be actual tuned headers, but they are coated and they look nice. ~$550.00<p>West Coast Fieros  http://home.earthlink.net/~chriswest/<br>Tuned headers, very nice.  $495 add $100 for ceramic coating.<p>FOCOA<br>http://www.fieroowners.com/store.html<br>I here they are ok, could be long wait to get them though.  $580, add $220 for coating.<p>RS Motorsports<br>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/<br>Ceramic coated header and ceramic coated downpipe.  That would be cool.  They want $1200 dollars "canadian", you do the math.<p>Fiero Heaven<br>http://www.fieroheaven.com/Headers.htm<br>Still dont know if they actually "have" these ready to ship.  Probably not coated but if they really can delivery these for less than $450 as they promised (by april??), than I guess it would be a good deal.<br>
Z||000003||Bruce||06-28-99||07:55 PM||||What is the best way to upgrade the present exhaust manifold, given the $500-600 cost of headers for the V-6? I've read here, somewhere, about polishing etc. What is involved in bringing the stock manifold up to its best performance level? Is it worth the effort?
Z||000004||mwbackus||06-28-99||08:38 PM||||You can find more info on exhaust manifold tricks here:<p>http://www.xnet.com/~nife/techtips/tt-exhaustmanifold.html<p>http://members.xoom.com/_XOOM/fierov6/OSG/exhaust-manifolds.html<p>For the money, I would say it is definatly worth it!!  If you are like me and would rather not mess with grinding on manifolds, I am sure that an auto machine shop could easily be found that would do the porting for less than $30.<br>
Z||000005||Bruce||06-28-99||08:45 PM||||Thanks! If I can just survive the ordeal of removing the manifolds, I'll just look up a good machine shop.
